+# OpenChatLink live conversation sync
+
+OpenChatLink imports personal ChatGPT and Claude web chats through Chrome, and
+local Codex desktop/CLI and Claude Code JSONL histories through a Phase Pal worker.
+The extension configures all four sources. No hstry database, Python process,
+or extra helper is needed for live sync. This feature is unreleased.
+
+## User setup
+
+1. Load the `phasepal-extension` folder in Chrome with Developer mode.
+2. Select the home character for new chats in Phase Pal. Enable Store Chat History.
+3. In Chat Settings > General > External Conversations, enable external sync.
+4. Copy the connection code into the extension and connect.
+5. Choose a source, load its titles, and select chats or explicitly choose all.
+6. Choose all history, the last 100 visible messages, or messages on/after a date
+   (00:00 UTC). Save automatic or manual scheduling separately for each source.
+7. Browser sources check once per minute with Chrome and Phase Pal running.
+   Local sources check about every five seconds while Phase Pal runs, including
+   after Chrome closes. Manual mode runs only when requested and continues in
+   bounded batches. Chats appear in the normal Chat History panel.
+
+Nothing imports until the user selects chats or chooses all. Selection is scoped
+by ChatGPT account, Claude organization, or local root. Choosing all Claude chats
+includes all available organizations. Title discovery does not import bodies.
+Deselection stops future updates and keeps the existing original. A nonempty
+limited window can shorten an original; no matching messages skip the import.
+
+## Identity, sharing, and replies
+
+There is one synced original per provider/account/conversation, with its first
+home character stored separately. Changing the pairing target affects new chats;
+reimporting an existing chat updates its original home without duplication.
+The runtime data path separates accounts, Steam channels, and Direct data.
+
+Share chats between characters changes history visibility and keeps the current
+chat when changing character. It does not change source identity, assignment,
+selection, or schedule. With sharing off, chats appear in their home groups.
+Character personality applies to new replies through its separate setting.
+
+Original transcripts are protected in both modes. Sending text first creates a
+local copy through the existing ChatV2 submit coordinator. Voice and edit actions
+require Continue in Phase Pal first. The banner names the source, explains that
+changes cannot sync back, and offers View synced original. Web sources also offer
+Open in ChatGPT or Claude. Local sources do not use an invented deep link.
+Copies have independent session/message IDs and can belong to another character.
+Core write guards and provider-dispatch guards protect originals. Whole-chat
+rename, pinning, and deletion remain available. Deleted originals stay deleted;
+unexpected local modifications cause conflicts instead of overwrite.
+
+## Local files and limits
+
+Codex reads `sessions` and `archived_sessions` under `CODEX_HOME`, or `~/.codex`.
+Desktop and CLI records use the same source identity. Claude Code reads `projects`
+under `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, or `~/.claude`. These environment variables must be set
+before Phase Pal starts. Network clients cannot supply filesystem paths.
+
+Only saved JSONL histories are supported. A valid prefix can sync while the final
+record is still being written. Remote-only or compressed histories require a
+separate adapter. Titles come from the first visible user message, rather than
+the Codex SQLite index. Source files are never modified.
+
+Scans reject linked paths and omit Claude Code subagent folders. Each source is
+bounded to 10,000 files/directories, depth 12, 64 MiB per file, 1 MiB per record,
+and 20,000 visible messages per chat. Changing a local root requires a new saved selection; it does not carry automatic
+import consent to that root. The reader caches title headers and checks
+file timestamps/lengths, skipping unchanged accepted snapshots. Each import pass
+handles at most 50 changed chats or 20 seconds, with cancellation. Manual requests
+persist through restart and continue in bounded passes. A failed manual pass
+requires Sync now again; automatic sources retry on later polls. The app reports
+read failures and size limits without paths or message content.
+
+## Ownership and receiver
+
+ChatV2RuntimeCompositionService creates the host-scoped external service against
+its raw history store. The existing ChatV2 host starts/resumes it on enable,
+suspends it on disable, and disposes it on destruction. The same lifetime owns
+the local task. All file, registry, socket, and secret work stays off frame paths.
+Generation and cancellation guards reject stale work. Completed IDs are published
+by Tick on Unity's thread; unchanged snapshots do not reload visible history.
+Disconnect in the extension pauses local collection. Disabling sync or revoking
+history consent in Phase Pal cancels both receiver and reader work.
+
+- IPv4 loopback only: `127.0.0.1:41771`, protocol `openchatlink/1`.
+- Health, ingestion, and local catalog/preferences/sync/pause routes require the
+  256-bit bearer credential. Website Origins are rejected; extension CORS is bounded.
+- Local routes allow only `codex` and `claude-code`; preferences reject unknown
+  fields, paths, and selections from another local root.
+- Text DTO sources are `chatgpt`, `claude`, `codex`, and `claude-code`, with a
+  conversation UUID, account/root scope, title, update time, and indexed messages.
+- Four clients, 16 KiB headers, 8 MiB HTTP bodies, depth 32, and 60-second request
+  cancellation bound receiver work. Transfer-Encoding and trailing JSON are rejected.
+- Pairing credentials use the existing scoped OS secret store. They are absent
+  from all JSON settings. The registry uses schema 2; local preferences use schema 1.
+  There is no migration or compatibility loader for earlier development imports.
+
+Only visible user/assistant text and timestamps are mirrored. Browser credentials,
+attachments, saved memory, system instructions, hidden reasoning, tool execution,
+and model state are excluded. No source write API is used. New replies use Phase
+Pal's selected provider and existing approval/cancellation rules.
+
+## Verification
+
+32 managed cases passed with production history stores, the HTTP receiver, and
+synthetic local JSONL files. They cover provider identity/navigation, selected-only
+body reads, incremental updates with a partial last record, independent copies,
+all/100/date limits, queued manual restart, authenticated local routes, rejected
+path input, host suspension, and history consent. 27 Node cases cover both web
+collectors and separate source controls, including Claude organization/branch
+isolation, bounded continuation, and failed-detail retry.
+
+Core, Runtime, Toolkit, and Platform compiled initially using available Unity
+reference assemblies. Core, Runtime, and Platform were recompiled after initial reader
+changes. The final receiver/reader components compiled directly in the managed
+harness when concurrent localization changes outpaced cached Unity references.
+A full current-worktree compile still needs refreshed references. No Unity process was
+launched and no personal conversations were accessed. These managed checks do
+not prove live web endpoints, Editor rendering, or packaged-player behavior.
+The offline Python fallback remains a separate ChatGPT-only flow.
